      "math_academy_id": "e-8554",
      "problem": "Given $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 37\\right),$ compute $P(X < 5).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14165669/assets/2fbe425a0c06a7b6dfdc97589a02523f60962cc1727fd5179bc73448fc0cd75c.svg)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac 37\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14165669/assets/3c72e913a8818b13b0237620960eaa87753058a84586d8d6ca9e2fdc5673148c.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4}{7})}^{0}(\\frac{3}{7})+{(\\frac{4}{7})}^{1}(\\frac{3}{7})+{(\\frac{4}{7})}^{2}(\\frac{3}{7})+{(\\frac{4}{7})}^{3}(\\frac{3}{7}) \\\\  & ≈0.893\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto  $3$ decimal places.",
